body:
Durability hardening stacked on Phase 26 PR #737.

Exact base:
`work/metaengine-rsi-paired-candidate-experiment-ledger-v1 @ 5d6f227bd8d97e9eb333d35a5ad66489a80361bf`

Exact head:
`work/metaengine-rsi-candidate-experiment-durable-v1 @ 75b423bdb4a223cd85a4dba2635664ceab431a75`

This closes two evidence-integrity gaps without changing Phase 26 authority or experiment semantics:

- ledger writes now build an immutable next-row preview, fsync + rename that preview, and only then publish it into live memory;
- a failed durable rename can no longer expose a phantom supported/rejected/inconclusive experiment in the running process;
- restart now revalidates the full persisted experiment intent policy instead of trusting a self-rehashed row;
- exact experiment identity is recomputed from source/request/plan/hypothesis, baseline/candidate artifacts, sealed tasks, harness, evaluator, trial-worker image, resource budget and task order;
- restart rederives paired metric regressions/improvements, validity blockers, environment/ambiguity state, eligibility, and ledger aggregate counts;
- self-rehashed policy weakening (including retry authority) and forged derived verdicts fail closed;
- focused regressions inject a durable rename failure and prove memory remains unchanged, then prove restart rejects policy/verdict forgery.

No trial execution, Browser effect, scheduler/task authority, candidate mutation, promotion, install, self-update, or automatic retry is introduced.

Verifier trust-root activation prepare stacked on Phase 24 PR #733.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-verifier-root-staging-v1 @ 2e47decd6b0d11a693c470ff3a748f6f922fff44

Research adaptation:
- Raft requires a two-phase/joint-consensus transition because direct old->new configuration switching can create conflicting majorities;
- etcd learner mode keeps a new member non-voting until it is caught up and safe to promote;
- etcd strict reconfiguration checks reject changes that could lose quorum;
- SPIFFE rotation overlaps old and new trust material before retirement.

Implements PREPARE only:
- consumes only an exact Phase 24 root-staging review with all PROMOTION/RUNTIME/TOURNAMENT propagation readbacks;
- candidate verifier remains LEARNER_NON_AUTHORITATIVE;
- predecessor verifier remains active throughout prepare;
- fixed readiness domains PROMOTION, RUNTIME and TOURNAMENT;
- each domain uses a precommitted external readiness root and independently verifies predecessor liveness, candidate catch-up, joint old+new validation, rollback path, root-history freshness, incident-free state and no pending effect;
- readiness also exact-binds the staged bundle digest and active predecessor root;
- candidate cannot vote, become active, self-promote or self-report readiness;
- all three readiness domains are mandatory;
- complete readiness yields only PREPARED_FOR_EXTERNAL_ROOT_ACTIVATION_COMMIT_REVIEW;
- activation_commit_token remains null; root_activation_commit_authorized=false and verifier_activation_authorized=false;
- existing hash-chained RSI runtime ledger records only the prepare-review evidence;
- candidate builder, tournament and promotion trust roots freeze the policy;
- no second scheduler, root ledger, executor or physical-effect plane is introduced.

No main merge, production mutation, verifier-root activation, Browser effect, promotion, signing, install or self-update is performed.

Stacked Phase 24 convergence slice on PR #729.

Exact base: work/metaengine-rsi-benchmark-coevolution-admission-v1 @ d2071646dbd6fa0a8302b8cd9ff44f4b99c5df5e

Selectively ports the useful cross-lineage experience-sharing semantics from PR #726 onto the stronger durable/provenance-grounded Phase 23 lineage, without keeping a second stale-base experience plane.

Preserved and strengthened semantics:
- shared lessons remain falsifiable evidence-backed hypotheses with exact origin provenance;
- counterevidence and a precommitted falsification test remain mandatory;
- only sanitized summary + distilled recipe digests may cross lineage boundaries; raw benchmark/verifier/hidden assets remain forbidden;
- source context, local revalidation protocol and negative-transfer probe are exact-digest bound;
- context compatibility, recipe verification and negative-transfer clearance are conjunctive external gates;
- recipient groups/scope remain externally assigned; candidate cannot expand scope, choose recipients, or suppress counterevidence;
- shared experience remains advisory only and consumers must revalidate locally while preserving source provenance;
- conflicting hypotheses remain preserved; no scalar winner is created.

Durability/replay hardening:
- new rows are validated into immutable preview state;
- preview is fsync+rename persisted before becoming visible in memory;
- failed persistence leaves row_count/eligible_count unchanged;
- restart independently reconstructs/validates hypothesis and admission policy instead of trusting self-rehashed rows;
- canonical summary fields are recomputed from rows and mismatch fails closed.

The bus cannot mutate skills, verifier, benchmark, scheduler or Browser state and cannot mark a hypothesis true.
No production mutation, Browser effect, scheduler, promotion, install or self-update.

Stacked RSI delayed post-deployment utility slice on top of PR #730.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-post-deployment-learning-v1-gpt @ 51cfb12290d9d050ca70839697a7a57ac8feea66

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-post-deployment-utility-v1-gpt @ 656f23f81fea9ca4ea706adcae84b42335960588

Implements delayed, externally evaluated utility for already persisted post-deployment Experience Graph cases:
- requires an exact persisted Phase17 post-deployment learning admission;
- minimum external observation window is 60 seconds and is bounded to 30 days;
- utility is HELPUL/HARMFUL/NEUTRAL through the existing Experience Graph utility receipt contract;
- exact target context is digest-bound to candidate/release/generation/environment/case/window/evaluator;
- candidate cannot self-rate, edit the prior case, mutate a candidate score or manufacture scalar reward;
- HARMFUL evidence remains queryable but cannot trigger rollback, self-update or promotion;
- utility appends to the existing Experience Graph without case replacement;
- graph mutation happens only after the utility event is durably appended;
- runtime restart replay validates and restores utility receipts;
- policy root is fenced from candidate mutation in isolated-builder, tournament and promotion roots.

No execution, release, self-update, rollback, scheduler, installer, command issue/lease/complete or production authority is added.

Stacked on confirmed release-authority/self-update review PR #728.

This adds a zero-authority admission envelope for the existing SelfUpdateRuntime.checkNow path:
- consumes only a persisted RSI self-update eligibility review;
- requires SelfUpdateRuntime v8 to be IDLE/CURRENT with no inflight download/install state;
- rejects CI test feeds and developer emergency bypass;
- requires HostResilience v7 ACTIVE with a healthy/ready Sentinel worker and no pending bootstrap retry;
- requires exact prior self-update transaction readback and rejects every unresolved state; only no prior, QUALIFIED, or SUPERSEDED are admissible;
- a QUALIFIED prior must describe the actually running current version;
- rejects attempts to reinstall the already-running target;
- the existing runtime must freshly resolve the trusted release again inside checkNow and reverify metadata before download;
- RSI persists only admission evidence and never calls checkNow itself;
- apply/restart/pre-install/installer handoff/installer launch all remain unauthorized;
- the admission adapter and HostResilience root are frozen from candidate mutation.

No updater check, network update effect, download, install, restart or self-update transaction is performed by this PR.

Verifier trust-root staging slice stacked on Phase 23 PR #725.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-verifier-root-change-review-v1 @ 08cde92c6e3dde86cd6cbdafe34ff888ac9ac8da

Research adaptation:
- SPIFFE recommends publishing new trust keys before use and retaining old keys until old credentials have drained;
- SPIFFE bundles use monotonic sequence numbers and keep trust-domain bindings distinct;
- TUF/Sigstore defend trust-root changes with monotonic/fresh metadata, threshold trust and rollback detection;
- in-toto separates immutable authorization layout from independently produced evidence.

Implements a stage-only overlap protocol:
- consumes only a Phase 23 root-change review that is READY_FOR_EXTERNAL_TRUST_ROOT_CONTROLLER_REVIEW;
- constructs a deterministic overlap bundle containing predecessor + candidate roots;
- predecessor remains the active verifier; candidate is staged/preloaded only;
- staging generation is exactly current generation + 1 and remains bound to the Phase 23 root-history digest and constitution;
- candidate-only bundles and predecessor retirement are forbidden;
- fixed validator domains are PROMOTION, RUNTIME and TOURNAMENT;
- each validator domain has a precommitted external validator root and must provide an exact external readback of bundle generation, bundle digest, overlap roots, active predecessor root and root-history digest;
- all three domain receipts are mandatory; duplicates cannot replace a missing domain;
- any early candidate activation, overlap loss, stale generation, bundle drift or history drift fails propagation;
- only complete exact propagation yields READY_FOR_EXTERNAL_ROOT_ACTIVATION_REVIEW;
- no root activation token is minted, root_change_authorized=false and verifier_activation_authorized=false;
- summary evidence is appended to the existing hash-chained RSI runtime ledger;
- candidate builder, tournament and promotion trust roots freeze the staging policy;
- no second scheduler, root ledger, executor or physical-effect plane is introduced.

No main merge, production mutation, trust-root actuation, Browser effect, promotion, signing, install or self-update is performed.

Stacked RSI post-deployment learning slice on top of PR #718.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-release-authority-convergence-v1-gpt @ 60c6dda93461bddb73fc01b8b8219366f85e2cd6

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-post-deployment-learning-v1-gpt @ 51cfb12290d9d050ca70839697a7a57ac8feea66

This closes the first verified deployment -> learning feedback loop without giving the learner release or execution authority.

Implemented:
- post-deployment learning requires a persisted EXTERNAL_RELEASE_AUTHORITY_CONVERGED Phase16 record;
- the running RSI source SHA must equal the externally converged candidate SHA, so an old parent cannot learn success on behalf of a successor;
- full upstream bindings are revalidated through convergence, effect reconciliation, release handoff and external promotion review;
- learning assignment must be external and candidate-authored=false;
- candidate self-reward, scalar reward and global score deltas are structurally forbidden;
- deployment success is admitted only as contextual experience, not global truth;
- exact candidate/release/authority/effect evidence is mapped into the existing append-only Experience Graph;
- graph mutation happens only after the learning event is durably appended;
- candidate cannot write/edit the graph or learning case;
- no raw trajectory/page/user/secret material is persisted;
- runtime restart replay now restores the previously missing Phase13-16 release-chain state and the new post-deployment learning state, validating each persisted object;
- post-deployment learning policy is fenced from candidate mutation in isolated-builder, tournament and promotion trust roots.

No release-authority mutation, self-update invocation, effect replay, scheduler, installer, command issue/lease/complete or production mutation is added.

Stacked Phase 23 RSI slice on PR #720.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-verifier-shadow-durable-v1 @ 49aa4e6c6730513f617351c0be531b7a13845f5e

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-benchmark-coevolution-admission-v1 @ d2071646dbd6fa0a8302b8cd9ff44f4b99c5df5e

Implements the research-frozen Phase23 benchmark coevolution boundary without creating a second provenance/evaluator plane:
- reuses the existing rsi-benchmark-provenance-guard and requires an exact ELIGIBLE_FOR_FULL_HOLDOUT_EVIDENCE admission;
- benchmark difficulty may advance only after an external mastery certificate;
- generation must advance exactly parent+1 and the proposed benchmark digest must change;
- active verifier root, trusted runtime, anchor set and held-out anchor remain stable across the append-only lineage;
- every generation requires external anchor recalibration;
- freshness, task-quality/broken-task, semantic construction, no-op ablation, environment-fidelity and agentic-usability audits are conjunctive gates;
- raw task content is excluded from the durable trust root; only exact typed digests/counts persist;
- process/outcome and controllable/environment failures remain separate;
- candidate cannot author/select tasks, sources, mastery policy, anchors, verifier, runtime or generation transition;
- a clean generation is only ELIGIBLE_FOR_SHADOW_BENCHMARK_TRIAL;
- current benchmark remains active and active verifier remains unchanged;
- append-only generation ledger is durable-before-memory, source-fenced, restart-verified, lineage-continuous and rejects grounding drift;
- benchmark coevolution policy is frozen in isolated candidate, tournament and promotion trust roots.

Research basis includes verifier-grounded benchmark coevolution, Building to the Test, OpenAI benchmark contamination/task-quality audits, Auto Benchmark Audit, Universal Verifier, Echoverse, AuditBench and Frontier-Eng.

No benchmark activation, verifier replacement, Browser effect, scheduler/task authority, promotion, install, self-update or production mutation authority is added.

Stacked on one-attempt RELEASE_PROMOTION journal PR #722.

This adds the next zero-authority transition after release promotion:
- consumes the exact persisted release-promotion journal intent plus externally produced Fabric events;
- requires terminal CONFIRMED outcome with independent readback; AMBIGUOUS is reconciliation-only and cannot advance;
- adds a typed external release-authority readback bound to effect id, journal digest, chain head, candidate SHA and observed authority SHA;
- candidate-authored authority readback is rejected;
- observed authority must be the exact frozen candidate SHA;
- trusted release is reverified again before any self-update consideration, including exact tag/version/source and installed-executable digest binding;
- emits only READY_FOR_EXTERNAL_SELF_UPDATE_CHECK_REVIEW;
- the existing SelfUpdateRuntime v8 and self-update transaction journal remain the sole install/update plane;
- prior transaction readback, restart gate and host resilience must be revalidated again by the external self-update controller;
- self-update check/apply/handoff, installer launch and physical replay are all explicitly unauthorized in this layer;
- runtime stores bounded digest-oriented eligibility evidence but never invokes the updater.

No release authority mutation, updater check, updater apply, installer handoff or physical effect is performed by this PR.

Phase 23 RSI trust-anchor review stacked on Phase 22 PR #719.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-verifier-shadow-qualification-v1 @ 33ad85c02032ef7b40a2f4fe533c9dd0f2ef4ffe

Research adaptation:
- TUF models root change as explicit trust-anchor metadata with threshold authorization and monotonic versioning;
- Sigstore uses threshold/offline trust-root holders, rotation, revocation and rollback/freshness defenses;
- in-toto separates an immutable authorized layout from produced evidence.

Implements:
- consumes only an exact Phase 22 QUALIFIED_VERIFIER_SHADOW chain;
- binds the frozen active predecessor root, proposed candidate root and independent secondary root;
- root generation must advance exactly by one; skips and rollback are rejected;
- root history is hash-chained through prior-history digest, old/new roots, qualification, fixed constitution and compatibility evidence;
- fixed compatibility manifest + compatibility evidence are digest-bound before approval;
- approvals are 2-of-2 from distinct PREDECESSOR_TRUST and SECONDARY_TRUST roles;
- the candidate verifier cannot approve itself;
- both approvals independently certify qualification binding, unchanged constitution, compatibility, rollback protection, root-history continuity, independent audit and shadow nonregression;
- disagreement fails closed;
- even dual PASS yields only READY_FOR_EXTERNAL_TRUST_ROOT_CONTROLLER_REVIEW;
- active verifier remains predecessor; no trust-root update token is minted; root_change_authorized=false and verifier_activation_authorized=false;
- the review summary is persisted in the existing hash-chained RSI runtime ledger;
- no second scheduler, root ledger, executor or physical-effect plane is created;
- candidate builder, tournament and promotion trust roots freeze this policy.

No main merge, production mutation, verifier-root actuation, Browser effect, promotion, signing, install or self-update is performed.

Stacked on immutable published-release reconciliation PR #703.

This implements the existing RELEASE_PROMOTION effect-domain boundary without adding a second publisher or scheduler:
- consumes only a durably persisted published-release reconciliation;
- creates a Browser Fabric INTENT before any authority exists;
- reuses the frozen RELEASE_PROMOTION ownership: RELEASE_PROMOTION_JOURNAL / RELEASE_PUBLISHER / RELEASE_PROMOTION_RECONCILER;
- requires an independently signed Ed25519 Browser Fabric capability exact-bound to effect id, candidate/previous authority incarnation, plan, policy, nonce and deadline;
- capability is single-use (max_uses=1), retry_budget=0 and delegation_depth=0;
- RSI and the candidate cannot mint the capability or invoke RELEASE_PUBLISHER;
- one physical ATTEMPT per effect is enforced by the shared Fabric ledger;
- CONFIRMED/ABSENT/CONFLICT/CORRUPT require independent exact readback;
- AMBIGUOUS permits only new readback + terminal reconciliation and explicitly forbids a second attempt;
- runtime persists only the pre-authority journal intent; capability admission/actuation remain external;
- release-promotion journal, capability verifier, effect ledger and effect-domain policy are frozen into candidate/tournament/promotion roots.

No release publication, authority mutation, self-update transaction or installer effect is performed by this PR.

Phase 22 RSI verifier-shadow qualification stacked on Phase 21 PR #716.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-verifier-evolution-admission-v1 @ bae80f7ea42a6f0894ff0c1470ada4f2c71c4cbc

Research-driven design:
- current evaluator-coevolution work shows anchored references plus held-out outer audits are necessary to prevent evaluator collapse;
- SLEIGHT-Bench shows monitor blind spots can be deliberately exploited;
- AuditBench shows static tool signal does not guarantee investigator/workflow success;
- sabotage evaluations show an overseer itself can undermine oversight;
- recent multi-judge work shows single judges have systematic capability-dependent bias, so disagreement is evidence but majority vote is not authority;
- monitorability results motivate measuring whether the challenger remains auditable under optimization pressure.

Implements a fixed hidden verifier-shadow audit matrix:
- exactly 16 externally audited cases, two each across ANCHOR, ADVERSARIAL_PROVER, REWARD_HACK, TRANSFER, TRAJECTORY, MONITORABILITY, SABOTAGE and WEAK_TO_STRONG;
- every case is stored only by digest/verdict/evidence references; no raw hidden case content is persisted or exposed to the candidate;
- exact Phase 21 eligible verifier-shadow admission is mandatory;
- reference verdict, predecessor verdict, candidate verdict and independent secondary verdict are recorded separately;
- secondary verifier must match the sealed reference on every case and evaluator-integrity + trajectory-replay checks must pass;
- candidate must match the sealed reference on every case;
- zero regression against the frozen predecessor is mandatory;
- at least one exact blind-spot repair (predecessor wrong, candidate right) is mandatory;
- no scalar score and no majority-vote winner can authorize qualification;
- qualification only yields QUALIFIED_VERIFIER_SHADOW and keeps the active verifier root on the predecessor;
- no verifier replacement/activation occurs; any future root change still requires a separate sealed admission;
- qualification summary is written to the existing hash-chained RSI runtime ledger; no second scheduler or authority ledger;
- candidate builder, tournament and promotion trust roots freeze the new policy.

No main merge, production mutation, Browser effect, verifier-root replacement, promotion, install, signing or self-update authority is introduced.

Stacked RSI release-authority convergence slice on top of PR #704.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-effect-result-reconciliation-v1-gpt @ 9e853366aef857446406f19ed39129fc7ef1d7fc

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-release-authority-convergence-v1-gpt @ 60c6dda93461bddb73fc01b8b8219366f85e2cd6

This slice does not advance release authority. It records only the evidence that the already-confirmed physical successor and an external release-authority journal have converged on the same exact release identity.

Requirements:
- prior Phase15 reconciliation must be CONFIRMED with exact qualified successor;
- exact trusted release version, candidate SHA and installed executable digest;
- independent external release-authority source readback;
- append-verified external authority journal entry;
- exact release tag/version/SHA/executable digest equality;
- successor Browser generation and external authority Browser generation equality;
- page/model output has zero authority.

Outputs:
- EXTERNAL_RELEASE_AUTHORITY_CONVERGED is an observation-only fact;
- no new authority store is created;
- RSI does not mutate the external authority journal/store;
- RSI does not advance release authority, invoke self-update, promotion, rollback or installer effects;
- post-deployment learning may consume the verified outcome only after this convergence record exists.

The new convergence root is immutable to RSI candidates and included in tournament/promotion roots. Runtime persists one convergence record per exact Phase15 reconciliation and replay-verifies it.

Stacked Phase 22 RSI slice on PR #715.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-sealed-verifier-evolution-admission-v1 @ 6eb986935d62e94c9d6cb880b921a4e7a504bc97

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-anchored-verifier-shadow-lifecycle-v1 @ 3934772774bc082739c2e578777f7668640c524e

Implements a verifier-shadow lifecycle without replacing the incumbent verifier:
- consumes only Phase 21 QUALIFIED_FOR_VERIFIER_SHADOW evidence;
- wraps candidate verifiers in a fixed trusted runtime outside candidate write authority;
- evaluates incumbent and candidate on an external anchor set plus a held-out anchor the candidate cannot read;
- requires a separate semantic construction audit and freshness probe;
- benchmark contamination, trusted-runtime drift, anchor-integrity failure, semantic-audit failure or any shadow metric regression blocks archive eligibility;
- at least one strict shadow-metric improvement is required;
- preserves multiple qualified verifier candidates in an append-only archive instead of selecting a scalar winner;
- records externally assigned specialty niches to preserve diverse stepping stones;
- incumbent verifier remains active;
- archive cannot gate canary, promotion, reward or Browser execution;
- candidate cannot self-archive, rewrite evidence or become active verifier;
- verifier-shadow lifecycle policy is frozen in candidate/tournament/promotion trust roots.

Research basis:
- Who Grades the Grader: anchored metric co-evolution with held-out audits;
- Microsoft Universal Verifier: benchmark the verifier itself and separate process/outcome + controllable/uncontrollable failures;
- verifier-grounded benchmark coevolution: fixed trusted runtime around mutable workflows;
- Darwin Godel Machine: preserve a diverse archive rather than greedy replacement;
- SWE-bench contamination and Building to the Test: freshness probes and independent semantic/construction audits.

No production verifier replacement, profile activation, Browser effect, scheduler, promotion, install or self-update authority is added.

Phase 21 RSI verifier-evolution slice stacked on sealed-canary generalization hardening PR #712.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-sealed-canary-generalization-v1 @ 70b3940b02863865c392b25598b370ff2b7796d8

Research-driven design:
- OpenAI prover-verifier games show verifier exploits should become adversarial training/evaluation data rather than being trusted away;
- weak-to-strong results show one weaker supervisor is not sufficient as sole recursive authority;
- current monitorability results support a separate monitor/evaluator path with additional test-time capability;
- recent metric co-evolution work indicates evolved evaluators need fixed anchors plus held-out outer audits;
- sabotage evaluations motivate explicitly evaluating whether the verifier itself can undermine oversight;
- recursive oversight/debate work motivates an independent secondary verifier and adversarial challenge suite.

Implements:
- verifier-evolution plans can only be created from a successful sealed canary review;
- frozen predecessor verifier root is taken from the exact sealed verifier receipt;
- candidate verifier root, predecessor root and precommitted secondary verifier root must all be distinct;
- hidden anchor, adversarial-prover, reward-hacking, transfer, trajectory-integrity, monitorability, sabotage and weak-to-strong suites are exact-digest bound before evaluation;
- candidate cannot choose/read hidden suites, choose the secondary verifier, change thresholds/stopping/risk budget or mutate the admission constitution;
- predecessor and independent secondary verifiers must evaluate the exact same plan;
- candidate-authored evaluation evidence is rejected;
- either verifier can reject; disagreement fails closed as REJECTED_VERIFIER_DISAGREEMENT;
- only dual PASS yields ELIGIBLE_FOR_VERIFIER_SHADOW;
- the active verifier remains the frozen predecessor; no root replacement or activation occurs;
- any future verifier-root change requires a separate sealed admission;
- admission receipt is persisted in the existing hash-chained RSI runtime ledger; no second scheduler, executor, or specialized authority ledger is introduced;
- candidate builder, tournament and promotion trust roots freeze the new admission policy.

No main merge, production mutation, Browser effect, live profile activation, verifier replacement, promotion, signing, install or self-update authority is introduced.

Stacked Phase 21 RSI slice on PR #711.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-external-readonly-canary-controller-v1 @ d74464f79cd12dc2b950baca270d4f0f585d97cf

Exact head:
work/metaengine-rsi-sealed-verifier-evolution-admission-v1 @ 6eb986935d62e94c9d6cb880b921a4e7a504bc97

Implements verifier evolution as a separate zero-authority lineage rather than allowing the improving system to rewrite its verifier in place:
- compares incumbent and candidate verifier on the same paired examples;
- keeps process-vs-outcome labels separate and controllable-vs-environment labels separate;
- requires sealed benchmark, transfer holdout, hidden reward-hack suite and independent external evaluator roots;
- compares false-positive rate, false-negative rate, reward-hack detection, environment-blocker calibration, process/outcome agreement and transfer agreement;
- any regression blocks qualification even if other metrics improve;
- at least one strict metric improvement is required;
- reward-hack exploitation, benchmark exposure, evaluator-integrity failure or replay failure block qualification;
- passing candidate is only QUALIFIED_FOR_VERIFIER_SHADOW;
- incumbent verifier remains active;
- verifier shadow cannot gate canary, promotion, reward, Browser effects or execution;
- append-only restart-safe ledger persists candidate verifier evidence;
- verifier-evolution policy is frozen in isolated-candidate, tournament and promotion trust roots.

No production verifier replacement, Browser effect, profile activation, scheduler, promotion, install or self-update authority is added.

Stacked convergence slice on durability hardening PR #705.

Exact base:
`work/metaengine-rsi-qd-shadow-comparison-durable-v1 @ 84193dd0e9b495aa78d998766442b7aea00d20a9`

Exact head at PR creation:
`work/metaengine-rsi-qd-canary-review-durable-convergence-v1-gpt @ c4917c58623f055b65539c41ccbd00a3485829cc`

This selectively converges the strongest compatible semantics from parallel RSI Phase19/20 lines without wholesale merging their selector/state planes:

1. PR #705 crash consistency remains the durable QD comparison base.
2. PR #707 QD review semantics are ported onto that durable base:
   - >=32 clean dual-plan comparisons;
   - >=4 verified contexts;
   - exact qualification/champion/challenger/comparator identity;
   - at least one meaningful SHADOW_DIVERGENCE;
   - fixed external cohort;
   - incumbent default + mandatory fallback;
   - output remains review-only, no canary token.
3. PR #702 multidimensional evidence semantics are selectively adapted to the QD lineage:
   - Outcome Safety;
   - Security Awareness;
   - Task Utility;
   - latency efficiency;
   - token efficiency;
   - no scalar winner.
4. PR #698/#710 safety-monitor semantics are carried into each external evidence row:
   - comparator integrity;
   - exact identity;
   - from-scratch replay;
   - security-negative check;
   - ambiguity and incident fail closed.
5. PR #709 anytime-valid review semantics are adapted without importing its alternate selector:
   - fixed independent recursive risk budget, global alpha 0.01;
   - E_VALUE_EXTERNAL_V1 or PAIRED_CONFIDENCE_SEQUENCE_EXTERNAL_V1 only;
   - familywise validity;
   - independent holdout;
   - precommitted stopping rule;
   - optional stopping forbidden;
   - certified noninferiority for Outcome Safety / Security Awareness / Task Utility plus material improvement.

A clean result is only `ELIGIBLE_FOR_EXTERNAL_BOUNDED_CANARY_CONTROLLER_REVIEW`.
It does NOT activate a canary, replace a live profile, issue Browser/tool effects, schedule tasks, install, self-update, sign or promote.

The new convergence root is frozen in isolated-candidate, tournament and promotion trust roots. Regression tests cover complete evidence binding, security/replay/identity/ambiguity/comparator/hard-invariant fail-close, risk-budget overrun, optional stopping, statistical rejection and zero-authority output.

Successor hardening slice on PR #706.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-sealed-canary-review-v1 @ 66aca21c5d9995576043dfa133d768ea4fcd5de7

This selectively converges the strongest non-duplicating post-canary verifier requirements discovered during the Phase 20 research pass:
- sealed canary review now requires an external transfer-holdout digest and PASS;
- sealed canary review now requires an external trajectory-integrity digest and PASS;
- candidate cannot choose either transfer holdout or trajectory-integrity suite;
- reward-hacking traps, sealed acceptance, transfer holdout and trajectory integrity are independent conjunctive gates;
- a positive mean utility and perfect self-authored tests cannot hide transfer/generalization failure;
- runtime threads both new evidence dimensions into the existing sealed review receipt and the existing hash-chained RSI ledger;
- no new ledger, scheduler, executor or authority plane is created;
- incumbent remains default and the result is still only eligible for later external promotion review through existing tournament/promotion gates.

Research basis:
- SEAL / self-authored-verification results require at least one deployment-acceptance signal outside the candidate's control;
- Verification Horizon argues fixed proxy verifiers saturate as generators improve;
- hack-verifiable environments motivate explicit trap suites for reward hacking;
